	(footprint "XIAO_RP2350_SMD"
		(layer "B.Cu")
		(uuid "2c343f96-e73f-4c35-9cac-eca39224a0bc")
		(at 58 36)
		(descr "Seeed Studio XIAO RP2350, 21x17.8mm, reflow/castellated (SMD) mounting. VENDORED VERBATIM from Seeed's own KiCad library -- github.com/Seeed-Studio/OPL_Kicad_Library, 'Seeed Studio XIAO Series Library/XIAO-RP2350-SMD.kicad_mod' -- with only the footprint NAME changed to match this file. Nothing here is eyeballed or measured off a photo, same rule as ModuleMountPads_Ring24. Pad map is from the matching Seeed symbol (Seeed_Studio_XIAO_Series.kicad_sym), not assumed: 1-11=D0..D10, 12=3V3_OUT, 13=GND, 14=VBUS, 15-22=D11..D18, 23=SWDIO, 24=SWDCLK, 25=EN, 26=GND, 27=BOOT, 28=3V3_OUT, 29=VBAT, 30=GND. Pads 15-30 are UNDERSIDE pads: they need copper keepout under the module even where unconnected. 3D MODEL: Seeed publish none for this part -- their KiCad library only references a private ${AMZPATH} library, and neither OSHW-XIAO-Series nor the wiki carries a STEP. XIAO_Module.step is therefore vendored from github.com/Tircown/ERCF-easy-brd (Kicad/ercf-easy-brd.pretty/packages3d/Seeeduino Xiao.step), which is GPL-3.0 and so compatible with this repo. It measures 17.80 mm across the pads -- the XIAO body width exactly -- and the family shares one outline, so it is the right body even though it is named for an earlier variant. VERIFIED against Seeed's OWN board file -- XIAO_RP2350_v1.0_SCH&PCB_240626.zip from files.seeedstudio.com, whose footprint-frame Edge.Cuts measures 20.955 x 17.780 mm; the model's PCB slab is 21.20 x 17.80, so +0.245 / +0.020 mm. Seeed publish the real STEP only behind a GrabCAD account: their KiCad library, their OSHW repo and even their own SCH&PCB project all reference a private ${AMZPATH} library (and Y:/01_Cadence_Library/) that ships nowhere. Transform is rot(90,0,180) offset(0,0,1.1): the STEP has Y as its height axis with the PCB slab at y 0..1.10 and the USB-C shell at y -2.17..0, x -11.90..-4.60, so it needs uprighting, a 180 spin to put the USB on +x where this footprint's silk shows it, and a 1.10 lift so the PCB sits ON the board instead of sunk into it.")
		(tags "xiao rp2350 seeed module")
